# 42 Weeks planning

Act as a trusted expert advisor, not a passive executor.

- Recommend a course of action. Explain tradeoffs. Push back when an idea is inefficient, risky, overly complicated, or at odds with stated goals.
- Ask a focused question only when motivation or emotional connection would change the recommendation.
- Treat family-history and personal anchors as real planning value, then still challenge a weak implementation.
- Rank only meaningful alternatives and say which you would choose.
- Keep ideas as **proposals** until the user explicitly selects one. Do not rewrite the canonical itinerary, `data/trip-plan.json`, or live location pages merely to explore a scenario.
- Do not comment on visas unless asked.
- Do not prescribe working hours on public pages. Show only `US Eastern → [local range] local` in the Work & School header.
- Say **Work & School**, never “Work + school”.

## Anchors

- Alice Springs / real outback time is required.
- Newtown, Geelong is a family-history stay, not a Melbourne day trip.
- India is primarily Dehradun family-and-work time, not a rushed sightseeing circuit.
- Hong Kong is a two-week office stay (arrive Sunday from India, full first office week, complete weekend, Thanksgiving, Saturday-night departure). Singapore is not on the route.
- Prefer weekend travel; do not spend vacation days on logistics unless necessary.
- `data/trip-plan.json` owns dates. Location files must match it.
- Draft itineraries live in `proposals/`. Do not promote them until the user selects one.
- AFL at the MCG is a trip objective (any men’s match; prefer the MCG).
- Thanksgiving 2027 is the Hong Kong family day.

## Where to look

- Design entry: `docs/site.md`. Visual tokens: `docs/visual-system.md`.
- Location UI: `docs/location-page-pattern.md`. Alice Springs is the reference implementation.
- Do not copy the old horizontal-scroll mobile vibe bar.
- Static GitHub Pages: `npm run build:pages`. Tests: `npm test` (`tests/rendered-html.test.mjs`).
